text:
The dish is a square plate, probably a side plate of about 20-22 cm. It holds roughly 12-14 roasted sweet potato cubes, each about 3 cm, so about 10-12 g each in volume terms is too low. At about 3x3x2 cm, each piece is around 18 cm³, or roughly 15-20 g. That gives about 13 × 15 g ≈ 200 g, though some pieces are smaller, so I'll use about 170 g.

Roasted sweet potato with a little oil comes to about 1.1-1.3 kcal/g. 170 g × 1.2 ≈ 200 kcal.

{"kcal": 200, "mass_g": 170}
